## Session summary

**Major win:** `cache_coherency` now **PASSES 4/4** (was the 7+ session blocker). The sess37 drain-pinned-bnobt fix (build `68DF68548A03059ED1292A6`), which I deployed this session, resolved it. No corruption on any node during 3× isolated `cross_write_read` + the full criterion run.

**Remaining blocker — root-caused and a fix implemented this session:**
`rsync_paired` reliably reproduced the recurring bnobt double-free (`ltbno+ltlen>bno` at xfs_alloc.c:2244 → FS shutdown). Per RULE 4, I instrumented rather than guessed:
- The sess37 pinned-drain fix path **never fires** under rsync (P73-FIX=0) → not the mechanism here.
- Decisive evidence: `P47-INACT inact_ino=131 incore_gen=G disk_di_mode=00 disk_di_gen=G+1 verdict=DISK-FREE`. The sess47 xfs_inactive guard fires correctly (14/5/4×) but has a **TOCTOU hole** — 2 double-frees slipped through. Two nodes both hold an nlink==0 inode in-core and race into destructive inactivation; the loser's point-in-time disk read saw it live, the peer freed it during the window, the loser double-freed.

**Fix (Gemini RULE-5 design, `notes/sess78_inactive_toctou_fix.md`):** In `xfs/xfs_inode.c::xfs_inactive`, acquire the per-inode **DLM EX** grant (low-level `mxfs_v5_dlm_inode_lock`, NOT ilock_begin — must not reload the VFS inode mid-eviction) BEFORE the disk-state guard read, hold it across truncate+ifree, release at `out:`. This serializes racing nodes so the loser's post-EX read sees di_mode==0 and skips → exactly-once destructive inactivation. DLM-then-ILOCK order is deadlock-safe (no ILOCK held in inodegc worker context).

**State:** Fix built as **`03CA6313F41BCA374D04703`**, deployed to all 4 nodes (all mounted clean). The validation `rsync_paired` run is in progress in the background (task `b7x40wjko`, log `/tmp/rsync_paired_run.log`).

**Next session:** Watch the bench result. Validation signals: no `ltbno+ltlen>bno`/P47 verdict=DISK-FREE; `rsync_paired` PASS. If clean, run full `verify_ship.sh` end-to-end (all criteria must pass in one run). If corruption persists, check whether the EX-acquire is actually serializing (add a P-INACT-EX-WON/LOST counter) and re-examine whether a non-inactivation path (rename/truncate) also frees stale-inode blocks.

